    "Frozen verify_inputs authenticates exact project/source snapshot and preregistered eight inputs, profile/config bytes and delivery reconstruction. Source root matches parent freeze; native request bytes and source policy match the frozen request.",
    "Public specification retains one Input object {n,m,a,b}; 0<=n<=500, m>0; a/b arbitrary signed unbounded integers. Floor rounds toward negative infinity and empty sum is zero. Canonical VSCore delivery and JSON shape replace only explicit delivery clauses; all preserved segments compare byte for byte. No additional input bounds are introduced.",
    "All seven original identities remain explicit. Source policy requires exact program.vscore.json/solve/arity1 and seven properties for O1,O2,S1,S2; value facets default true, with only approved S1/S2 source-only. Assumptions/exclusions/non-vacuity stay separate.",
    "Fresh frozen challenge source (not accepted proof authority) defines Input.n/m/a/b as Int and valid_input exactly 0<=n and n<=500 and 0<m. Its reference solve uses Int.fdiv(a*Int.ofNat i+b,m), List.range(n.toNat) and List.sum, preserving signed floor and empty sum.",
    "Fresh challenge binds O1/O2 to complete_behavior: forall valid_input x, solve x equals the complete explicit floor sum, conjoined with Source.Contract SolveSource. S1/S2 bind operational_source to the same exact source requirements. A required separate valid_input_inhabited theorem proposes n=0,m=1,a=0,b=0. Challenge proof holes remain normal pending obligations; no acceptance is inferred."
  ],
